---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Morgan Henley Presents | About">
	<main class="about-page">
		<header class="about-heading">
			<p class="eyebrow">The people behind the night</p>
			<h1>Community<br /><em>is the headliner.</em></h1>
		</header>
		<div class="about-grid">
			<div class="about-lead">
				<p>Morgan Henley Presents was founded in the Summer of 2016 in the Snoqualmie Valley, WA. We produce music events designed to bring together community, musicians, artists, businesses, and other like-minded people.</p>
				<p class="about-callout">Small towns.<br /><span>Big energy.</span></p>
			</div>
			<div class="about-copy">
		<p>
			Morgan Henley Presents was founded in the Summer of 2016 in the Snoqualmie
			Valley, WA. Morgan Henley Presents is a production company specializing in
			producing music events. The goal is to bring together community,
			musicians, artists, businesses & other like minded people through these
			events. The owner & operator, Morgan Henley, has 13 years of experience in
			the PNW music & entertainment scene. Morgan was a partner in
			BrodiesProductions (2006-2010) & People w/ Instruments (2011-2016) before
			venturing out on his own. Currently, MHP is involved in a number of Summer
			events in the Snoqualmie Valley: Duvall Days, Carnation 4th of July
			Celebration, Railroad Days (Snoqualmie, WA), Carnation Block Party - Rock
			the Nation, & the longest running music festival in The Snoqualmie Valley,
			BrodieNation Music Festival. More coming in the Summer of 2019.
			BrodieNation was the 1st event production of Morgans career. Started in
			2006 w/ his best friend & co-owner of BrodiesProductions, Alexander
			“Kainoa” Turner, the festival that started as a “Party” has progressed
			into a little gem of a micro music festival. Check out <a
				href="http://www.brodienation.com">brodienation.com</a
			> for more details. MHP has produced & currently produces events at a number
			of Snoqualmie Valley venues. Such as: The Bindlestick (Snoqualmie), Pete’s
			Club Grill (Carnation), Twin Dragon Sports Bar (Duvall), Snoqualmie Falls Brewing
			(Snoqualmie), Red Pepper Pizza (Carnation) & most recently the historic North
			Bend Theatre. For information on upcoming North Bend Theatre shows visit www.northbendtheatre.com.
			There’s also new venues outside of the Snoqualmie Valley in the works for 2019.
			One being a Winter concert series @ the Snoqualmie Summit. More details coming
			soon. Follow the action on Instagram <a
				href="https://www.instagram.com/morganhenleypresents/"
				>@morganhenleypresents</a
			>" & <a href="https://www.instagram.com/brodienationmusicfest/"
				>@brodienationmusicfest</a
			>"
		</p>
		<p>
			For inquiry or booking questions please visit <a href="#home"
				>www.morganhenleypresents.com</a
			>
			or email <a href="mailto:morganhenleypresents@gmail.com"
				>morganhenleypresents@gmail.com</a
			>.
		</p>
		<p>
			Morgan Henley is also involved in other community ventures. Including
			being a board member & radio show host on the local Snoqualmie Low Power
			FM station Valley 104.9. For more details please visit www.valley1049.org
			& like us on Facebook @ <a href="https://www.facebook.com/valley1049/"
				>facebook.com/valley1049/</a
			>". To listen to the most eclectic 2 hours of radio you’ve ever heard
			check out The Jammies w/ Morgan Henley. Airing every Friday night from
			7pm-9pm. Stream live from the Valley 1049 website or on TuneIn. You can
			also listen on <a href="https://soundcloud.com/the_jammies_morgan_henley"
				>soundcloud.com/the_jammies_morgan_henley</a
			>. Like the show on Facebook @ <a
				href="https://www.facebook.com/JammieswMorganHenley/"
				>facebook.com/JammieswMorganHenley/</a
			>
		</p>
		<p>
			A new venture Morgan is a part of is The Lee Arts Foundation in Carnation.
			An arts foundation in memory of the late Lee Grumman. More info to come
			about that in 2019.
		</p>
		<p>
			Here’s a list of events & venues Morgan Henley has worked with during
			BrodieProductions & People w/ Instruments.
		</p>
		<h2 class="bio-list-header">BrodieProductions</h2>
		<ul>
			Waldos (Kirkland, WA)<br />
			Valhalla Bar & Grill (Kirkland, WA, Produced the 1st BeerPong tourney in a
			bar in WA)<br />
			Night Club (Seattle, WA)<br />
			Lake Street Bar & Grill (Kirkland, WA)<br />
			I Immigrant (Seattle, WA)<br />
			Floyd’s Place (Seattle, WA)<br />
			Pete’s Club Grill (Carnation, WA)<br />
			Music Festival 2006-2012 (Carnation, WA).<br />
		</ul>

		<h2 class="bio-list-header">People w/ Instruments</h2>
		<ul>
			Created & Produced PWI Music Festival 2012 & 2013 (Carnation, WA)<br />
			Co-Produced Homegrown Music Festival 2014 (Carnation, WA)<br />
			Co-Produced NW Roots Festival (Carnation, WA)<br />
		</ul>
		<h2 class="bio-list-header">Venues</h2>
		<ul>
			Pete’s Club Grill (Carnation, WA)<br />
			Twin Dragon Sports Bar (Duvall, WA)<br />
			Raging River Cafe (Fall City, WA)<br />
			The Pour House (North Bend, WA)<br />
			The Bindlestick (Snoqualmie, WA)<br />
			The Rolling Log Tavern (Issaquah, WA)<br />
			Nectar Lounge (Seattle, WA)<br />
			BrodieNation Music Festival 2012-2015 (Carnation, WA)<br />
		</ul>
			</div>
		</div>
	</main>

	<style>
		.about-page { max-width: 1180px; margin: auto; padding: 6rem 2rem 2rem; }
		.about-heading { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); padding-bottom: 4rem; }
		.about-heading .eyebrow { color: var(--acid); }
		.about-heading h1 { margin: 2rem 0 0; color: var(--paper); font-family: var(--serif); font-size: clamp(4rem, 10vw, 9rem); font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: -0.09em; line-height: 0.78; }
		.about-heading h1 em { color: var(--acid); font-style: normal; }
		.about-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 0.8fr 1.2fr; gap: 8rem; padding: 5rem 0; }
		.about-lead > p:first-child { margin: 0; color: var(--paper); font-size: 1.2rem; line-height: 1.45; }
		.about-callout { margin-top: 8rem; color: var(--cobalt); font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 3.5rem; font-style: italic; letter-spacing: -0.07em; line-height: 0.8; transform: rotate(-5deg); }
		.about-callout span { color: var(--coral); }
		.about-copy { color: var(--paper-muted); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.7; }
		.about-copy p { margin: 0 0 1.5rem; }
		.about-copy a { color: var(--acid); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
		.bio-list-header { margin: 3rem 0 1rem; color: var(--paper); font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.75rem; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; }
		.about-copy ul { margin: 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; color: var(--paper-muted); font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.72rem; line-height: 1.8; }
		@media (max-width: 750px) {
			.about-page { padding: 4rem 1.25rem 1rem; }
			.about-grid { display: block; padding: 3rem 0; }
			.about-callout { margin: 4rem 0; }
		}
	</style>
</Layout>
